    "summary": "Segundo (bass) drum; the body is made of hollowed-out trunk of Santa Maria hardwood; the drum head is white-tailed deer skin, held in place by a circle of vine and tied down by twisted plastic (polyethylene) rope; wooden dowels or pins are threaded through rope to tighten the drum head; plastic (polyethyelene) knotted string crosses over the drum head. The drum is painted with a yellow, white and black Garifuna flag on one side and a scene of the re-enactment performed on Garifuna Settlement Day (19th November).",
